  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">El Salvador malaria elimination: a country effort - El Salvador (01-Jan-2017-30-Jun-2020)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">El Salvador, Malaria, Ministry of Health of the Republic of El Salvador (MOH)This program has the following goals: To strengthen the multisectoral and sustainable national response with comprehensive actions that are integrated with health promotion, illness prevention, community participation, caring for the environment, health care, epidemiological and entomological monitoring, to eliminate autochthonous malaria and promote favorable living conditions for the population.. The objectives of this program are: To ensure national and multisectoral political commitment to the Eliminaci&#xf3;n de la Transmisi&#xf3;n Aut&#xf3;ctona de la Malaria [elimination of the indigenous transmission of malaria - ETAM]..  To promote access to and universal coverage of early diagnosis, radical cure treatment, follow-up and rehabilitation of malaria cases..  To strengthen integrated vector management with a cross-sectoral approach and community participation for the prevention and elimination of malaria..  To strengthen laboratory, treatment and epidemiological monitoring systems, integrated within the SHIS for the analysis and interpretation of the epidemiological behavior of malaria..  To strengthen the health care system with malaria elimination activities.</narrative>
  </description>
